0..43 Comment "//! Rose trees use direct and mutual forms."
44..47 Comment "//!"
48..89 Comment "//! `Bush` stores its children in `List`."
90..134 Comment "//! The list parameter is strictly positive."
135..191 Comment "//! Its measure maps over the children at a lower stage."
192..245 Comment "//! A run passes `map` the children\'s type as a code."
246..249 Comment "//!"
250..296 Comment "//! `Rose` and `Forest` form one mutual block."
297..363 Comment "//! Their measures are one fixpoint over the sum of their domains."
364..417 Comment "//! Each measure is that fixpoint at its own summand."
418..472 Comment "//! The mutual measures keep a later weight parameter."
473..527 Comment "//! Each recursive call uses a smaller tree or forest."
528..531 Comment "//!"
532..600 Comment "//! - see: #3722 — a measure keeps a parameter in its sibling call"
601..627 Comment "//! - see: #517 — `Bush`"
628..655 Comment "//! - see: #393 — `nodes`"
656..704 Comment "//! - see: #452 — `shrub_nodes`, `grown_nodes`"
705..752 Comment "//! - see: `../../pathological/data/rose.gandr`"
753..809 Comment "//! - cites: [Abel-2004-termination_checking_with_types]"
810..813 Comment "//!"
814..938 Comment "//! [Abel-2004-termination_checking_with_types]: https://doi.org/10.1051/ita:2004015 \"Abel, Termination checking with types\""
